:{},"asterisked":[],"paragraphs":{"codes":{},"covered":{"1":"The correct use of an ICD-10-CM code listed below does not assure coverage of a service. The service must be reasonable and necessary in the specific case and must meet the criteria specified in this determination. The following ICD-10-CM Diagnoses codes are used in conjunction with 92132 (anterior segment) only.","2":"The following ICD-10-CM Diagnoses codes are used in conjunction with 92133 (posterior segment-optic nerve) only.","3":"The following ICD-10-CM Diagnoses codes are used in conjunction with 92134 and 92137 (posterior segment, retina) only. C79.49* should be used only for secondary malignant neoplasm of the choroid. The following diagnosis codes were added to support the medical necessity of CPT code 92134, effective for services rendered on or after 8/1/2019: H33.301, H33.302, H33.303, H33.311, H33.312, H33.313, H33.321, H33.322, H33.323, H33.331, H33.332, H33.333","4":"ICD-10-CM codes Z79.899*and Z03.89* are intended to be reported with CPT code 92134 (Spectral Domain-OCT modality only) for patients who require long term use of chloroquine (CQ) and/or hydroxychloroquine (HCQ) only. *Use Z03.89 when testing is necessary prior to chloroquine (CQ) and hydroxychloroquine (HCQ)therapy. *Use Z79.899 and Z09 to report testing due to the use of chloroquine (CQ) and/or hydroxychloroquine (HCQ). *Use Z03.89 when testing is necessary prior to GILENYA&trade; (fingolimod) therapy. *Use Z79.899 and Z09 to report testing due to the use of GILENYA&trade;(fingolimod) therapy."},"noncovered":{}}}]